    "m2_prompt_trader_proposal_original": "**Action**: Hold\n\n**Reasoning**: The evidence supports maintaining the current JPM position rather than adding or selling. The trend is unambiguously up \u2014 JPM is at all-time highs, 25% above its 200-day SMA in a golden cross configuration, up 17.5% over 60 days with a shallow 1.2% drawdown, and the balance sheet is strong ($327.9B equity, positive operating cash flow, active capital return). However, the leading indicators are rolling over (RSI fell from 79.41 to 71.01 in a single day, MACD histogram contracted two consecutive days), the March 22 candle is a textbook shooting star at all-time highs, and the stock is statistically stretched (9% above the 50-day SMA vs. a typical 3-5% range). With zero forward visibility into the mid-April Q1 earnings report and no macro or sentiment data in the evidence, chasing at 186.56 is poor risk-reward. The honest synthesis is a genuine Hold \u2014 the bull cannot justify chasing at stretched levels with momentum decelerating, and the bear cannot justify selling a strong, fundamentally sound uptrend on a single reversal candle.\n\n**Entry Price**: 183.44\n\n**Stop Loss**: 179.79\n\n**Position Sizing**: Moderate weight; do not concentrate. Reserve dry powder to add on pullback toward 10 EMA (183.44) or Bollinger middle band (179.79).\n\nFINAL TRANSACTION PROPOSAL: **HOLD**",
